y showcase their hard work... Event Details » First-Year Experience for Faculty Columbia College is excited to welcome new faculty to campus. We've specifically designed a year of support that: Provides orientation to the life of a faculty member at Columbia College Supports your teaching and scholarship with professional development Creates a community of support for future teaching, scholarship, service, and leadership at Columbia College Ongoing Support First-Year Faculty Lunches with the Provost Monthly gatherings of all first-year faculty take place for a time of sharing about faculty experiences. Invited guests may also participate to discuss topics of interest and explore opportunities taking place on campus. Lunch is provided by the Provost's office. When : 12:30- 1:20 p.m. (Common Hour) on select Thursdays throughout the semester. Peer Mentor Learning Community Faculty will become members of small mentor learning groups to share experiences and provide support across the first year (and beyond). Each community is expected to meet as a group at least twice a semester, and guidance from Faculty Development will be provided to include observation and discussion resources. Each member is to partner with another to complete peer observations. When : Twice a semester on select dates throughout the semester. Virtual Monthly Minutes 15-minute brown bag lunch virtual chats will provide information on topics to support new faculty at Columbia College. These will be recorded and shared with new faculty unable to attend. Topics include: August - Campus-wide Student Support  September - Major and General Education Requirements When: 12:30 - 12:45 p.m. (Common Hour) on select dates throughout the semester. October - Sticky Teaching Situations Panel November - Supporting Academic Integrity & Policies January - Establishing a Scholarly Agenda February - Faculty Governance, Service, and Advocacy March - Teaching, Service, and Research Balance April - Understanding the Evaluation Process Campus-Wide Professional Development Series A set of monthly learning opportunities with fellow colleagues designed to foster community while building the capacity of our faculty and staff. When : 12:30 - 1:20 p.m. (Common Hour) on select dates throughout the semester. Growing & Thriving Campus \"With our growth comes the need to expand academic offerings by adding to our already exceptional team of educators so that we may better serve our student body. I am thrilled to welcome new faculty members to the Columbia College family as we seek to equip our students with the tools they need to live lives of impact.\" Dr. Kristine Barnett Program Director, Higher Education Administration Coumbia College 800.277.1301 1301 Columbia College Drive Columbia, SC 29203 Directions Campus Map Footer Current Students Academic Calendar Academic Bulletin Koala Connection Login Canvas Login Webmail Accessibility Quick Links Directory Employment Library Registrar Compliance Privacy Social Links Facebook Instagram Linkedin Twitter Youtube Legal Compliance Privacy Policy Copyright © 2026 Columbia College. Website by Cyberwoven . Sitemap"
