to Apply Open How to Apply Undergraduate Online & Undergraduate Online Graduate Honors Admissions International High School Counselors How to Transfer Admissions Team Accepted Students Orientation Open Orientation Launch Tuition & Aid Open Tuition & Aid Tuition & Cost Financial Aid Open Financial Aid Cost of Attendance Cost of Attendance Financial Aid Dictionary & FAQs Scholarships & Grants Veterans Benefits Student Life Open Student Life Compete in Esports Competitive gaming can build your leadership, critical thinking, and technical skills. One of the hottest trends on college campuses is flourishing right here. Esports Feature Student Life Housing Dining Health & Wellness Student Organizations Explore Columbia Student Handbook Athletics Open Athletics Athletics Advertising Athletics Advertising Champions of Character Recruiting Process About Open About Accreditation Open Accreditation QEP SARA Compliant Process & Professional Licensure Higher Education Relief Funds Higher Education Relief Funds Consumer Information Family Educational Rights & Privacy Act (FERPA) Employment Events Faculty & Staff Directory Give Us Feedback Give Us Feedback History Leadership Open Leadership Board of Trustees Office of the President Open Office of the President On the Rise: Strategic Vision On the Rise: Strategic Vision Office of the First Lady Mission, Vision & Values News & Stories Open News & Stories Find an Expert Media Information Online Map Online Map Header Nav Koala Community Open Koala Community Current Students Open Current Students Registrar Open Registrar Academic Calendar Commencement Graduation Requirements Student Affairs Open Student Affairs Diversity, Equity & Inclusion Counseling & Case Management Bookstore & Koala Pantry Campus Information Open Campus Information Facilities Request Campus Safety Tuition Payments Faculty & Staff Parents & Families Alumni Open Alumni Give Open Give Faculty/Staff Giving Donor Recognition Planned Giving 50th Reunion Giving Alumni Association Alumni Events Alumni FAQs Columbia Community Open Columbia Community Event Spaces Goodall Gallery Women's Business Center Community Engagement Mascot Program Breadcrumb Home Academics Undergraduate Degrees Teaching Fellows Teaching Fellows Welcome, Future Teacher Fellow! Columbia and Newberry College will provide a unique, inclusive experience for each incoming Teaching Fellow through a truly collaborative approach. Both schools are well-established, innovative, and highly respected institutions and are positioned to make history as the first collaborative program in the state. How to Apply The SC Teaching Fellows application is hosted by Kaleidoscope and serves as the first step in the rigorous identification process for Teaching Fellows. The application submission window is open from October 1st until December 1st. Test scores, transcripts, and reference surveys must be submitted by December 7th. Students must apply for Teaching Fellows during their final year of high school. Eligibility To apply for Teaching Fellows, you must be: a U.S. citizen or will be an eligible non-citizen under State Residency Statutes at the time of high school graduation (Please note - students categorized as Deferred Action for Childhood Arrivals (DACA) are not eligible for Teaching Fellows.) a legal resident of South Carolina (Please note - Residency will be verified by the Teaching Fellows Institution after a student has been offered an award.) a high school senior or junior graduating early Being a Fellow While enrolled in the Teaching Fellows Program, students must: maintain continuous progress toward SC teacher certification; successfully complete 30 semester hours per academic year (or maintain status as a freshman with 30 completed hours, a sophomore with 60 completed hours, a junior with 90 completed hours, or a senior with 120 completed hours); maintain a minimum cumulative Teaching Fellows Institution (TFI) GPA of 2.80 ​​ ; be accepted into the TFI's Teacher Education Program by their junior year; remain a full-time student during each fall and spring term; attend Teaching Fellows programs as assigned by the institution; and attend enrichment programs as assigned by the institution and CERRA. Why Teaching Fellows? The Teaching Fellows Program is available at 14 colleges and universities across the state. Each Teaching Fellows Institution (TFI) has a Campus Director who works closely with the cohort of Fellows throughout their higher education experience. Teaching Fellows participate in enrichment programs, have professional development opportunities, are involved with S.C. communities and businesses, and receive up to $6,000 in annual fellowships for four years while completing a degree leading to initial teacher certification. The total possible fellowship of up to $24,000 provides up to $5,700 annually for tuition, board, and direct education expenses and up to $300 annually for planned enrichment programs. Funds not used in fall or spring semesters due to other scholarships or funding sources can be used for Maymester or summer school, but only during the same academic school year. Why Columbia College? Becoming a Columbia College Teaching Fellow provides a unique opportunity to participate in a series of innovative courses and school-based field experiences designed to greatly enhance an aspiring teacher's potential as a future educator and leader. Some highlights are: Access to resources at both Columbia College and Newberry College Completion of a Public Policy Internship in agencies that support public education Attendance at state-wide Teaching Fellows Conference sponsored by CERRA Aunnual visits from the SC Teacher of the Year Student-selected Inquiry Research Project presented during American Education Week Partnership/outreach to local Teacher Cadet sites another Teaching Fellows institutions Learn More About the CERRA Application Academics Undergraduate Degrees Open Undergraduate Degrees Pre-Professional Tracks Honors Program Call Me MISTER CREATE Teaching Fellows Online Undergraduate Degrees & Certificates Online Graduate Degrees Certificates Academic & Career Support Open Academic & Career Support Accessibility & Accommodations Career Services Tutoring Learning Commons at Edens Library Open Learning Commons at Edens Library Edens Library Mastery Lab Tutoring Pearce Communication Center Resilience Institute Partnership with Newberry College The South Carolina Teaching Fellows Program administered by CERRA: Recruits talented high school students for the teaching profession in SC Provides up to $24,000 (up to $6,000 a year/up to $5,700 for tuition and board and $300 for specific enrichment programs administered by CERRA) in Fellowship funds to pursue a degree leading to initial teacher certification Includes personal and professional development, service and enrichment opportunities Requires graduates to teach in a SC public school one year for every year they participate in the program How to Apply A True Collaboration I chose Columbia College for my Teaching Fellows Institution because of the personalized attention and endless opportunities given to every single student. The professors were committed to me becoming the best teacher I can possibly be. The small size of the cohort made it ideal for establishing meaningful bonds among peers. We participated intravel, leadership, and recreational experiences together. Our professors knew us so well that they invited us into their homes for gatherings. You don't get that level of personal involvement at a larger institution. Most importantly, Columbia College Teaching Fellows program gave me the experience, tools, and confidence to be a successful leader in the classroom. The Teaching Fellows Program is designed to cultivate leadership qualities and provide meaningful opportunities for future educators. At Columbia College, leadership development and student experiences are at the heart of our vision. As the Campus Director of the Teaching Fellows Program, I am excited to offer teacher candidates the same transformative opportunities I received as a Teaching Fellow at Columbia College—experiences beyond the classroom that opened doors I never thought possible. Collaborating with Newberry College will further expand access and possibilities, doubling the impact we can have on our future teachers. Sara Monts Teaching Fellows Alumnae - Dance Education Kirsten Baker Teaching Fellows Alumnae, Middle Level Education Keisha Pearson Teaching Fellows Campus Director A Supportive Community Our Division of Education team is here to help you become the best teacher you can be. Keisha Pearson Lecturer of Education Dr. Tracy West Dean of the School of Education | Professor of Special Education Connect With Us Have more questions about Teaching Fellows or applying to Columbia College? We're thrilled you're interested and excited to discuss our unique program with you. Email Us Apply to Columbia College Coumbia College 800.277.1301 1301 Columbia College Drive Columbia, SC 29203 Directions Campus Map Footer Current Students Academic Calendar Academic Bulletin Koala Connection Login Canvas Login Webmail Accessibility Quick Links Directory Employment Library Registrar Compliance Privacy Social Links Facebook Instagram Linkedin Twitter Youtube Legal Compliance Privacy Policy Copyright © 2026 Columbia College. Website by Cyberwoven . Sitemap"
