ciation Alumni Events Alumni FAQs Columbia Community Open Columbia Community Event Spaces Goodall Gallery Women's Business Center Community Engagement Mascot Program Breadcrumb Home Academics Academic & Career Support Career Services Career Services Career Services provides resources and programs for students and alumni to develop the necessary skills to conduct effective career searches and make informed career decisions. Including: Individualized Career Guidance and Planning Graduate School Assistance Professional Development Workshops Resume Critiques Mock Interviews Internship Assistance Employment Fairs and Employer Information Sessions Appointments Career Services is available for walk-ins and by appointment. Appointments may be made for in-person visits, or virtual visits via Zoom. Please note, for walk-ins, staff may not always be available. To check availability, please use the Navigate app or the lobby kiosk in the J. Drake Edens Library. To make an appointment, please use Navigate. NAVIGATE Columbia College's Career Platform Students and Employers use Koala Careers, Columbia College's career platform for connecting students to services and employers. Students can set up an account using their Columbia College credentials and use Koala Careers to find a variety of career opportunities, including internships, workshops, events, and other career-related programs. Koala Careers Koala Careers partners with Indeed to provide students with access to the Indeed Job Search Academy. From résumé and interview tips to job search strategies and career advice, these resources are designed to help you confidently pursue internships and full-time employment. Register for an Indeed account to unlock these free career development tools. Indeed Job Search Academy Through Koala Careers, students receive free access to LinkedIn Learning's extensive library of expert-led online courses. Develop in-demand skills, strengthen your résumé, prepare for interviews, and explore professional development opportunities. Simply sign in with your Columbia College email address to get started. LinkedIn Learning Career Exploration Resources WHAT CAN I DO WITH THIS MAJOR CAREER INTEREST ASSESSMENT PERSONALITY ASSESSMENT SKILLS MATCHING ASSESSMENT WORK VALUES MATCHING ASSESSMENT Contact Us Location: Career Services is located in the Edens Learning Center Commons. Hours: Monday - Friday | 8:30 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. Academics Undergraduate Degrees Open Undergraduate Degrees Pre-Professional Tracks Honors Program Call Me MISTER CREATE Teaching Fellows Online Undergraduate Degrees & Certificates Online Graduate Degrees Certificates Academic & Career Support Open Academic & Career Support Accessibility & Accommodations Career Services Tutoring Learning Commons at Edens Library Open Learning Commons at Edens Library Edens Library Mastery Lab Tutoring Pearce Communication Center Resilience Institute Coumbia College 800.277.1301 1301 Columbia College Drive Columbia, SC 29203 Directions Campus Map Footer Current Students Academic Calendar Academic Bulletin Koala Connection Login Canvas Login Webmail Accessibility Quick Links Directory Employment Library Registrar Compliance Privacy Social Links Facebook Instagram Linkedin Twitter Youtube Legal Compliance Privacy Policy Copyright © 2026 Columbia College. Website by Cyberwoven . Sitemap"
