 Open How to Apply Undergraduate Online & Undergraduate Online Graduate Honors Admissions International High School Counselors How to Transfer Admissions Team Accepted Students Orientation Open Orientation Launch Tuition & Aid Open Tuition & Aid Tuition & Cost Financial Aid Open Financial Aid Cost of Attendance Cost of Attendance Financial Aid Dictionary & FAQs Scholarships & Grants Veterans Benefits Student Life Open Student Life Compete in Esports Competitive gaming can build your leadership, critical thinking, and technical skills. One of the hottest trends on college campuses is flourishing right here. Esports Feature Student Life Housing Dining Health & Wellness Student Organizations Explore Columbia Student Handbook Athletics Open Athletics Athletics Advertising Athletics Advertising Champions of Character Recruiting Process About Open About Accreditation Open Accreditation QEP SARA Compliant Process & Professional Licensure Higher Education Relief Funds Higher Education Relief Funds Consumer Information Family Educational Rights & Privacy Act (FERPA) Employment Events Faculty & Staff Directory Give Us Feedback Give Us Feedback History Leadership Open Leadership Board of Trustees Office of the President Open Office of the President On the Rise: Strategic Vision On the Rise: Strategic Vision Office of the First Lady Mission, Vision & Values News & Stories Open News & Stories Find an Expert Media Information Online Map Online Map Header Nav Koala Community Open Koala Community Current Students Open Current Students Registrar Open Registrar Academic Calendar Commencement Graduation Requirements Student Affairs Open Student Affairs Diversity, Equity & Inclusion Counseling & Case Management Bookstore & Koala Pantry Campus Information Open Campus Information Facilities Request Campus Safety Tuition Payments Faculty & Staff Parents & Families Alumni Open Alumni Give Open Give Faculty/Staff Giving Donor Recognition Planned Giving 50th Reunion Giving Alumni Association Alumni Events Alumni FAQs Columbia Community Open Columbia Community Event Spaces Goodall Gallery Women's Business Center Community Engagement Mascot Program Breadcrumb Home Academics Learning Commons At Edens Library Tutoring Tutoring Tutoring & Academic Support Services Your Success Starts with Support At Columbia College, we believe that every student can excel when given the right tools, guidance, and encouragement. Our Academic Support and Tutoring Services are designed to help you strengthen your skills, master course material, and gain confidence in your academic journey. Whether you’re on campus or online, our tutors and staff are here to help you thrive. Academic Support During the Semester Tutoring and academic coaching remain available throughout the fall semester, though capacity may vary. Once an appointment is scheduled, you’ll receive instructions on how to prepare and make the most of your session. We encourage all students, from first-year to senior, to take advantage of these free services early in the semester to stay ahead, build better study habits, and achieve lasting success. Tutoring Services at the Pearce Communication Center (PCC) Located in the lower level of Edens Library , the Pearce Communication Center supports student excellence across written and oral communication, reading comprehension, and study methods. Our trained tutors provide one-on-one and small-group support to help you improve clarity, organization, and confidence in your work. Get help with: Writing assignments and research papers Speech preparation and presentation skills Reading and comprehension strategies Study techniques and time management To schedule an appointment: Visit Navigate to request a tutor or book a session. Business, Math, and Sciences Tutoring Center Located in Room 126 of the Barbara Bush Center for Science and Technology , this center provides a supportive learning environment for students enrolled in Biology, Business, Chemistry, Computer Information Systems, and Mathematics courses. Tutors can assist you with: Understanding key concepts and formulas Preparing for quizzes and exams Building study and test-taking strategies Reviewing class material and homework To schedule an appointment: Visit Navigate to find available sessions and times. Support for Online Students If you’re taking courses remotely and have questions or concerns, we’re here for you, too. Our Distance Learning Support Team helps resolve online course issues quickly to ensure your success and confidence in virtual learning. Need help? Submit your concerns here , and a member of our Columbia College staff will review your request and reach out with support. Why Students Use Tutoring Services Build confidence in challenging subjects Improve time management and organization skills Learn new study strategies tailored to your learning style Receive personalized feedback in a supportive environment Strengthen academic performance and long-term success Every student deserves to feel confident and capable. Let’s make your next study session the one that gets you there. Academics Undergraduate Degrees Open Undergraduate Degrees Pre-Professional Tracks Honors Program Call Me MISTER CREATE Teaching Fellows Online Undergraduate Degrees & Certificates Online Graduate Degrees Certificates Academic & Career Support Open Academic & Career Support Accessibility & Accommodations Career Services Tutoring Learning Commons at Edens Library Open Learning Commons at Edens Library Edens Library Mastery Lab Tutoring Pearce Communication Center Resilience Institute Coumbia College 800.277.1301 1301 Columbia College Drive Columbia, SC 29203 Directions Campus Map Footer Current Students Academic Calendar Academic Bulletin Koala Connection Login Canvas Login Webmail Accessibility Quick Links Directory Employment Library Registrar Compliance Privacy Social Links Facebook Instagram Linkedin Twitter Youtube Legal Compliance Privacy Policy Copyright © 2026 Columbia College. Website by Cyberwoven . Sitemap"
